# wear/man/coat_stride: the coat skirt's knee rows in side views, keyed by the legs (motion rebuild, 2026-10-21,
# docs/MOTION_P2.md 7.3). coat_hang.pxm's side rest views stop above row F-6; these views put those rows back for every
# standing leg key the side views draw with hang=rest (pixel for pixel, so idles, postures and swings compose as before),
# and draw the pass keys (walkB2, walkD2) with the hem lifted, so both knees show as the legs cross. GARB (motion rebuild).
# Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body man
role garment coat
layer hangFront
anchor hip
keys legs
z 1

view R key idle origin 7 -4
|555555555555
build
|...+x.......

view R key guard origin 7 -4
|555555555555
build
|...+x.......

view R key buckle origin 7 -4
|555555555555
build
|...+x.......

view R key lunge origin 7 -4
|555555555555
build
|...+x.......

view R key stance origin 7 -4
|555555555555
build
|...+x.......

view L key idle origin 6 -4
|5555555555555
build
|........x+...

view L key guard origin 6 -4
|5555555555555
build
|........x+...

view L key buckle origin 6 -4
|5555555555555
build
|........x+...

view L key lunge origin 6 -4
|5555555555555
build
|........x+...

view L key stance origin 6 -4
|5555555555555
build
|........x+...

view D key idle origin 0 0
|.

view U key idle origin 0 0
|.

view D key guard origin 0 0
|.

view U key guard origin 0 0
|.

view D key buckle origin 0 0
|.

view U key buckle origin 0 0
|.

view D key lunge origin 0 0
|.

view U key lunge origin 0 0
|.

view D key stance origin 0 0
|.

view U key stance origin 0 0
|.


view R key walkB2 origin 5 -1
|58877677791
build
|..+x.......


view R key walkD2 origin 5 -1
|58877677791
build
|..+x.......


view L key walkB2 origin 7 -1
|1988777766665
build
|........x+...


view L key walkD2 origin 7 -1
|1988777766665
build
|........x+...

# MAN-WEAR (P2B rollout, 2026-10-22): the stride panel states its intent on every side walk and run key. The reach keys
# (walkB2, walkD2) carry the skirt row coat.pxm's side run views no longer draw (they end at the tunic's hem, so the legs'
# hipline is judged where the tunic's is); the contact and down keys draw nothing (coat_hang's wide view carries that row
# and the knee rows lift with the stride) and neither do the run keys (the flare carries the skirt). The front and back
# views of those keys draw nothing either, exactly as before.

view R key walkA origin 0 0
|.

